      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "The Taylor series for the function $f(x)$ about $x=0$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{3n}{x}^{n-1}.\n$$\n\nCalculate the first three non-zero terms of the Taylor series expansion about $x=0$ of ${f}^{′}(x).$",
      "worked_solution": "Writing the first few terms of the series explicitly, we have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{3n}{x}^{n-1}=-\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{6}x-\\frac{1}{9}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{12}{x}^{3}-⋯.\n$$\n\nTo find ${f}^{′}(x),$ we differentiate term-by-term. This gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=0+\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{2}{9}x+\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}-⋯.\n$$",
